5BSD contributed software register
==================================

Record new third-party imports and upstream refreshes here. Keep upstream
sources separate from native build integration where practical. An entry
must identify the source directory, upstream project and release or revision,
source URL and archive SHA256 (or exact upstream commit), license files and
exceptions, local changes, build/install scope, and update instructions.
Update the entry in the same change as the import or refresh. Preserve the
upstream notices and review file-specific licenses, including files omitted
from the installed system.

Also record upstream-derived tests, implementation examples and behavioral
references used in native code outside contrib/. For each addition, identify
the pinned upstream files, local destination files and whether code was
copied/adapted or independently implemented from observed behavior. Update
this register in the same change; source comments alone are not the register.

Fuchsia Starnix Linuxulator references
--------------------------------------
Recorded: 2026-10-10
Upstream: https://fuchsia.googlesource.com/fuchsia
Revision: 8a938a3224e768f6254ee12d240b6492361ebccf (inventory snapshot;
  the earlier pidfd regression revision is recorded separately below).
Source root at that revision: src/starnix/
Browse: https://fuchsia.googlesource.com/fuchsia/+/8a938a3224e768f6254ee12d240b6492361ebccf/src/starnix/
Archive: https://fuchsia.googlesource.com/fuchsia/+archive/8a938a3224e768f6254ee12d240b6492361ebccf/src/starnix.tar.gz
Reviewed archive SHA256:
  bbfd58bc2350014e439a62fb250ff7bc94901a30f27ae2ff637960711de943e6
Scope: behavioral reference and test ideas rewritten as freestanding Linux
  syscall probes and native 5BSD fixes. No Starnix Rust/Zircon implementation
  is imported or linked by this work. This revision is separate from the
  FIDL/lowpan source import. The reviewed archive was extracted under
  /tmp/starnix-inventory-8a938a32; that temporary path is not a durable source.
License/notices: reviewed Starnix files carry The Fuchsia Authors copyright
  notices referring to the upstream root LICENSE (BSD-style). Consult LICENSE
  and PATENTS at the pinned revision and each file's notices before copying
  source text; retain applicable notices for any subsequent code adaptation.
  contrib/fuchsia/LICENSE and PATENTS belong to the separately pinned import.

Upstream-to-local mappings (upstream paths relative to src/starnix/;
local paths relative to the 5BSD source root):
  - kernel/core/vfs/syscalls.rs, close_range table detachment:
    sys/compat/linux/linux_file.c, linux_file.h and linux_fork.c;
    sys/kern/kern_descrip.c and sys/sys/filedesc.h;
    tests/sys/kern/linux_break_files.c and linux_unshare.c.
    Native guarded table-copy implementation and independent regression
    tests; Starnix's per-task table model is a behavioral reference.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/task_test.cc, clone/exec sharing:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_unshare.c and sys/kern/kern_exec.c.
    Rewritten CLONE_FILES detachment/CLONE_FS preservation tests and a native
    exec correction. tools/test/linuxulator/guest-gate.sh selects the cases.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/epoll_test.cc and kernel/core/vfs/syscalls.rs:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_break_epoll.c and sys/compat/linux/linux_event.c.
    Rewritten MOD-data, alias-self, poll-readiness and invalid-wait tests;
    native result-buffer address-range validation prompted by these tests.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/pidfd_test.cc:
    Original regression reference recorded in the local test:
    c6af7c1ef9a32cc236e98c31f37151b9e40e9540.
    https://fuchsia.googlesource.com/fuchsia/+/c6af7c1ef9a32cc236e98c31f37151b9e40e9540/src/starnix/tests/syscalls/cpp/pidfd_test.cc
    tests/sys/kern/linux_break_pidfd.c and sys/compat/linux/linux_misc.c.
    Rewritten waitid WNOHANG siginfo/rusage regression with additional PID
    and nonblocking PIDFD cases; native no-event siginfo correction.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/procfs_test.cc, DynamicFileSeek/PastEnd:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_procfs.c, cmdline seek and past-EOF test ideas.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/io_uring_test.cc and modules/iouring/io_uring.rs:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_io_uring_reference.c. Rewritten setup-flag and
    READV/WRITEV reference tests, extended with invalid setup checks.
    Local round trip submits sequentially; it does not reproduce upstream's
    simultaneous-submission ordering case or import its ring backend.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/inotify_test.cc:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_inotify_starnix.c and linux_inotify_starnix_test.sh.
    Five rewritten upstream test scenarios plus a local open-directory
    lifetime guard. Initially child-before-parent was an expected failure.
    Follow-up: Linux 6.12.110-0-lts runtime confirms that ordering. The native
    vfs_inotify.c adapter now emits terminal events for Linux directory watches
    before the parent notification when only the operation's reference remains.
    Other active references and regular files retain inactive-time deletion.
    Added held-directory parent-order and cwd lifetime guards; all eight cases
    pass in the Linux reference guest. New 5BSD runtime remains pending; the
    ATF expected-failure annotation was removed.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/socket_test.cc, GetsockoptTruncationTest:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_sockopt.c and sys/compat/linux/linux_socket.c.
    Rewritten option-length/prefix/canary tests, extended to send timeouts and
    NEW timeout variants; native legacy timeout copyout truncation fix.
    Follow-up: the same test method now covers SO_ERROR, SO_DOMAIN,
    SO_LINGER and TCP_USER_TIMEOUT in the separate translated_truncation
    ATF case, compiled from linux_sockopt.c with SOCKOPT_TRANSLATED_ONLY=1.
    All four native translation paths now use the existing truncating helper.
    Behavior was also checked against Linux v6.12 sk_getsockopt and
    do_tcp_getsockopt (reference only; no Linux source text copied):
    https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/net/core/sock.c
    https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/net/ipv4/tcp.c
    Those Linux files carry SPDX GPL-2.0-or-later notices. This follow-up
    extends locally written tests and uses the existing 5BSD copyout helper.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/input_test.cc GetDeviceName and ioctl_test.cc
    EVIOCGNAME_Success/EVIOCGNAME_TooSmall:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_evdev_starnix.c, linux_evdev_fixture.c and
    linux_evdev_starnix_test.sh; sys/compat/linux/linux_ioctl.c.
    Rewritten zero-length and truncated-name tests, extended locally to
    physical/unique strings and untouched trailing bytes. The native uinput
    fixture creates its own device. The adapter bypasses generic ioctl's
    zero-size rejection and copies only the evdev-reported string length.
    Uses Linux prefix truncation, preserving the upstream test's explicit
    distinction from Starnix's truncated-string NUL termination.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/terminal_test.cc ioctl_TCSETSF and PacketMode:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_terminal_starnix.c and its ATF wrapper.
    Rewritten terminal cases with a stronger queued-input flush check,
    packet header-only read, retained payload and packet-mode disable.
    No native TTY implementation change in this batch.
  - tests/syscalls/cpp/fuse_test.cc HeaderLengthUnderflow and
    OverlongHeaderLength: tests/sys/fs/fusefs/bad_server.cc.
    Three locally written framing cases exercise declared lengths zero,
    less than the header and greater than the actual write. Preserve native
    malformed-session termination; upstream's retry-on-same-session behavior
    is not claimed. No FUSE kernel change in this batch.
    Subsequent local audit: sys/fs/fuse/fuse_device.c now checks daemon errno
    bounds before negation, avoiding signed overflow for INT32_MIN in both
    Linux errno translation and native reply completion. Six additional
    BadReplyErrno cases in bad_server.cc cover negative extremes and positive
    reply errors in both errno modes, preserving existing request behavior.
    This is a local follow-up, not copied Starnix implementation code.
  - Pre-Binder follow-up (2026-10-10), same pinned Starnix revision:
    input_test.cc CurrentStateQueriesSucceed and capability-query tests:
    linux_evdev_starnix.c adds zero-size and bounded-copy bitmap checks.
    linux_ioctl_evdev now bounds bitmap copyout, including the native empty
    force-feedback bitmap. Native state and capability storage are reused.
    uinput_test.cc UiGetVersion, UiSet*bit, UiSetPhys, UiDevSetup/Null,
    UiDevCreateFailedWithoutDevSetup and create/destroy cases:
    linux_uinput_starnix.c and ATF wrapper are rewritten validation/lifecycle
    tests; linux_ioctl.c/h now translate supported uinput commands to the
    native backend. Force-feedback is explicitly unsupported. UI_GET_SYSNAME
    returns the native event-node name with Linux length/termination rules.
    terminal_test.cc PacketModeEvents: adds a rewritten packet-event case
    and a local /dev/ptmx nonblocking-open regression. The latter exposed
    dropped FNONBLOCK in sys/dev/pty/pty.c; the clone-open path now retains it.
    procfs_test.cc UptimeProgressSeek/UptimeProgressReopen and
    ProcSysKernelRandomBootIdExists: linux_procfs_starnix.c adds rewritten
    refresh checks and a stronger UUID format/stability check.
    fuse_test.cc LookupUpdatesExistingNodeAttributes: lookup.cc adds
    second_name_refreshes_cached_inode using existing native mock helpers.
    Linux v6.12 evdev/uinput source used only to check ABI behavior (no GPL
    implementation text copied):
    https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/drivers/input/evdev.c
    https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/drivers/input/misc/uinput.c
    Licenses there: GPL-2.0-only and GPL-2.0-or-later respectively.
    Inotify ordering audit also consulted Linux v6.12 fs/namei.c
    (vfs_rmdir) and include/linux/fsnotify.h (d_delete_notify); reference
    only, no code copied. URLs:
    https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/fs/namei.c
    https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/include/linux/fsnotify.h
    Runtime comparison remains necessary; pinned Starnix expectations are
    not assumed universal across Linux versions/filesystems.
    Also inspected the same fsnotify helper at Linux v7.1. A reference-only
    Alpine Linux v3.22 netboot kernel was downloaded for isolated qualification
    (no source imported or guest booted; local QEMU lacks libusb.so.4):
    https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/v3.22/releases/x86_64/netboot/vmlinuz-lts
    SHA256 49eac7bf8cedfd316897bef805111616f3d2855492ee7870e82cb1e6a88c7572
    Stored at /tmp/starnix-linux-reference/vmlinuz-lts.
    socket_test.cc SndRcvBufSockOpt.DoubledOnGet also guided a temporary
    native-baseline probe in /tmp/starnix-linux-reference/socket-buffers.c;
    persistent tests and buffer accounting changes are still pending.
  - Additional pre-Binder option work (2026-10-10), same Starnix revision:
    uinput_test.cc UiDevCreateTouchscreenWithSize informs axis readback in
    linux_uinput_starnix.c: the adapter accepts short UI_ABS_SETUP prefixes,
    zero-fills omitted fields, rejects oversized requests/invalid axes/ranges
    and limits MT slots. A new abs_setup ATF case verifies readback through
    the native event node; it uses Linux axis values, not Fuchsia display
    coordinate remapping. Linux v6.12 drivers/input/misc/uinput.c was an ABI
    reference for request sizes and validation (no code copied).
    socket_test.cc SndRcvBufSockOpt.DoubledOnGet:
    tests/sys/kern/linux_socket_buffers.c and its ATF wrapper add four socket
    family/type combinations, dup alias checks, zero/min/max/negative sizes,
    failed-set preservation and unprivileged force-option rejection.
    linux_setsockopt_buffer in linux_socket.c reserves doubled native space,
    bounded by sb_max_adj and native mbuf minima; native quota checks remain.
    No Linux CAP_NET_ADMIN grant exists (capget reports no capabilities), so
    forced setters return EPERM instead of silently acting as normal setters;
    forced getters return ENOPROTOOPT. Privileged Linux force support is not
    claimed. Minima/ceilings follow native storage/accounting, not fixed Linux
    skb sizes. Linux v6.12 net/core/sock.c and include/net/sock.h were consulted
    for normalization, clamping, force permissions and set-only semantics:
    https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/net/core/sock.c
    https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/include/net/sock.h
    Reference only; no GPL source text copied.
  - Linux reference qualification follow-up: 18/18 inotify/socket/procfs/TTY
    cases passed on the downloaded Alpine 6.12.110-0-lts kernel in a diskless,
    networkless QEMU guest using tmpfs. This supersedes the earlier QEMU
    dependency blocker and resolves the source-only inotify ordering concern.
    QEMU loaded a private copy of libusb.so.4 from
    /usr/obj/5BSD-linuxgate/run-20261009T202958Z/root-amd64/usr/lib/libusb.so.4;
    no host library was replaced. Inputs/source hashes and console output:
    /tmp/starnix-linux-reference/results.json and console-final.log.
    Reference execution found a timing assumption in the rewritten TCSETSF
    test: linux_terminal_starnix.c now waits for POLLIN before checking the
    line-discipline input count. This is a local test correction.
  - FUSE directory parser follow-up (2026-10-10), same pinned revision:
    modules/fuse/lib.rs FuseOperation::parse_response(Readdir) informed a
    bounds review of sys/fs/fuse/fuse_internal.c. Validate namelen before
    aligned-record sizing so oversized names cannot masquerade as EOF.
    tests/sys/fs/fusefs/readdir.cc adds six malformed/truncated wire-record
    cases, checking the next request retains offset zero, and one successful
    MAXNAMLEN boundary case. These are newly written native regressions, not
    copied upstream tests. Native partial-tail short-read semantics remain;
    Starnix instead rejects incomplete records with EINVAL. No Rust code was
    copied. READDIRPLUS cache population/reference ownership remains open.
    modules/input/uinput.rs ioctl and tests/syscalls/cpp/uinput_test.cc
    UiSetPhys were also checked: pinned Starnix UI_SET_PHYS simply succeeds
    without storing its argument. It does not provide an implementation for
    our remaining native 80-byte physical-name storage limit.
  - READDIRPLUS implementation follow-up (2026-10-10), same pinned revision:
    modules/fuse/lib.rs FuseFileObject::readdir and
    FuseOperation::parse_response(Readdir) supply the behavioral model:
    negotiated PLUS/AUTO selection, offset-zero AUTO policy, bounded aligned
    records, cache prefill even after the caller's buffer fills. Native code
    in fuse_internal.c/fuse_ipc.c/h uses the existing vnode, namecache,
    attribute cache and FORGET backend. fuse_node.c/h adds nonblocking vnode
    acquisition for optional prefetch; the vfs_hash_insert error path now
    respects that helper's existing reclaim/release ownership. No Rust or
    Zircon code was copied. Native dot/zero-nodeid semantics, ENOSYS fallback,
    cookie preservation and nonblocking-cache behavior are local integration.
    tests/sys/fs/fusefs/readdir.cc adds 15 newly written PLUS cases;
    mockfs.cc audits the new opcode. Tests cover alias/FORGET accounting,
    dot/zero nodeids, AUTO/old protocol/ENOSYS, small user buffers, EFAULT,
    invalid cache names, invalid lengths followed by valid entries, and six
    malformed framing cases. Kernel/test builds do not establish VM acceptance;
    teardown of unparseable replies, vnode races, cache TTLs and NFS cookies
    remain in Desktop/Fuchsia tests for next VM.txt.
  - FUSE option/concurrency follow-up (2026-10-10), same pinned revision:
    readdir.cc adds busy_vnode_returns_reference_without_waiting, a native
    regression for the nonblocking prefetch integration. It holds a GETATTR
    reply pending, checks PLUS completes and returns its unused reference,
    then checks reclaim returns only the original LOOKUP reference.
    The PLUS test count is now 16. This test is locally written.
    modules/fuse/lib.rs FuseFs::rename / FuseOperation::Rename serialization
    references the RENAME2 wire layout, but Starnix sends flags zero there.
    Native fuse_internal.c/h, fuse_vnops.c and fuse_ipc.c now implement
    NOREPLACE through RENAME2 for protocol 7.23+, using the Linux flag value
    already defined in sys/compat/linux/linux_file.h. Daemon EEXIST survives;
    ENOSYS is remembered and returns EOPNOTSUPP without a destructive legacy
    fallback. Native rename.cc adds six rewritten RPC/atomicity/error cases;
    mockfs.cc/h audits the new request. No Starnix/GPL code was copied.
    Poll audit: FuseFileObject::query_events requests kh=0/flags=0 and its
    wait_async returns None; tests/syscalls/cpp/fuse_test.cc FuseTest.Poll
    checks immediate readiness. These are not asynchronous notification
    support. Splice audit: Starnix advertises SPLICE flags, while native
    Linuxulator buffered splice needs FUSE frame/error ownership work before
    those flags can be advertised. Findings and VM gates are recorded in
    docs/starnix-linuxulator-inventory.md and the Desktop checklist.
  - Cache lifetime and VM-gate follow-up (2026-10-10), same pinned revision:
    tests/syscalls/cpp/fuse_test.cc FuseServerCacheAttributesTest.CacheAttributes
    supplied the attribute-cache lifetime model. Three newly written native
    Timeouts/ReaddirPlusCache.honors_cache_lifetimes cases exercise PLUS with
    zero attribute TTL, zero entry TTL, and finite entry TTL expiration;
    expired names may resolve to a different inode and all lookup references
    must be reclaimed. PLUS coverage is now 19 cases. No upstream code copied.
    tools/test/linuxulator/fuse-protocol-manifest.py and the revised
    qemu-fuse-protocol.py/guest-fuse-protocol.sh qualify exact case names and
    kernel/module/test SHA256s instead of a historical fixed pass count.
    The build helper now uses every logical CPU. These are local test tools,
    not imported Fuchsia implementations. test-fuse-protocol-gate.py checks
    rejection of incomplete, duplicate, stale and failed/skip evidence.
    Current manifest: 48 native GTest programs, 885 active cases; generated
    at /tmp/starnix-fuse-protocol-20261010-cache.json. This is build/listing
    evidence only, not a claim that 885 cases ran in a VM.
  - Native vnode teardown review (2026-10-10): fuse_node.c now respects
    insmntque()'s failure ownership contract as well as vfs_hash_insert()'s.
    insmntque clears v_data and reclaims/releases the vnode; FUSE must not
    assert or unlock that released vnode. The error path instead destroys
    the private attribute mutex, frees private data and balances the node
    counter. This is a native integration fix found while reviewing PLUS
    prefetch/forced-unmount lifetime; no upstream implementation was copied.
    Matching GENERIC kernel/modules built and were staged with NO_ROOT=yes
    in /usr/obj/5BSD-starnix-fuse-vm-20261010/root for isolated validation.
    No host kernel/module installation or reboot was performed.
  - Native FUSE bootstrap review (2026-10-10): the isolated VM exposed a
    pre-INIT root GETATTR deadlock from mac_veriexec_vfs_mounted. Native
    fuse_vnop_getattr now supplies uncached owner-only bootstrap root
    attributes, including the same local fsid used after INIT. This follows
    the native pre-INIT statfs model, not copied Starnix implementation.
    GetattrBeforeInit.root_attributes_are_not_cached checks mount completion
    before INIT and daemon-provided root mode/link count after INIT. The
    existing mock's INIT helper is exposed for this delayed-INIT test.
    Full mounted validation remains required; initial failure/stack evidence
    is in /usr/obj/5BSD-starnix-fuse-vm-20261010/diag-console.log.
    Native fixture integration explicitly answers system.mac_abac GETXATTR
    queries with ENOATTR (Linux ENODATA for linux_errnos mounts), representing
    an unlabeled test filesystem while retaining active MAC policy. Other
    xattr requests remain subject to normal per-test expectations.
    Full native VM run-2 completed 881/886 active cases, including all 19
    READDIRPLUS and six NOREPLACE additions. Follow-up fixture corrections:
    malformed framing checks ENXIO for a new LOOKUP on an already-dead native
    session (in-flight requests still use ENOTCONN); default_permissions
    matches the requested user.foo xattr instead of consuming policy queries;
    Death.unsent_operations warms name/label caches and polls the daemon fd
    for the queued second request before killing the daemon, replacing a
    scheduling-dependent sleep. These are native integration/test fixes.
    Run-3 reached 885/886 passes; a policy query could still precede a
    path-based OPEN. The death regression now uses direct reads on two
    already-open files, retaining the dispatched/queued split and strict
    ENOTCONN checks without path-label interference.
    Native run-4 now passes all 886 active GTest cases with matching artifact
    hashes, active MAC policies and clean ZFS shutdown. Evidence:
    /usr/obj/5BSD-starnix-fuse-vm-20261010/run-4. The separate Linuxulator,
    device and extended teardown gates remain open. The local
    guest-starnix-prebinder-atf.sh stages no upstream implementation; it runs
    the seven selected ATF programs on ZFS/tmpfs in a disposable guest.
    VM qualification follow-up: those seven wrappers explicitly brand their
    freestanding Linux ELF probes with brandelf -t Linux and declare that
    tool dependency. They previously relied on a host fallback-brand sysctl
    that a clean VM does not enable. Native evdev fixtures remain native.
    The guest driver accepts built-in uinput and stages Kyua/ATF runtime
    data plus resolved compiler headers. No Starnix code was copied for
    these harness corrections; results remain in the Desktop VM checklist.
    The first branded ATF run passed 27/28 cases on ZFS and exposed missing
    EV_SYN in Linux EVIOCGBIT(0). Native evdev accepts synchronization events
    independently of its advertised type bitmap, so linux_ioctl_evdev now
    exposes that implicit support in nonempty event-type replies. The existing
    bitmap-bounds regression fails at check 120 before this fix; the native
    fixture deliberately does not request EV_SYN. Pinned Starnix input_file.rs
    also omits this bit; Linux input_register_device is the behavioral check:
    https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux/+/8934827db5403eae57d4537114a9ff88b0a8460f/drivers/input/input.c
    This is an independently written ABI translation, not copied GPL code.
    Rebuilt-kernel VM qualification remains required.
    Follow-up qualification completed: atf8-results.json verifies all 56
    selected ATF executions on ZFS/tmpfs, including the EV_SYN fix; run-5
    verifies all 886 native FUSE cases on the rebuilt kernel. Both retain
    exact hashes and clean shutdown evidence in the same VM directory.
    Additional earlier Linuxulator gates and teardown diagnostics remain open.
  - FUSE vnode type-replacement lifetime follow-up (2026-10-10):
    reviewing the native LOOKUP path alongside READDIRPLUS exposed a retained
    reference from vfs_hash_get when an inode changes type. vgone reclaims
    the vnode but does not release that reference; fuse_node.c now uses
    vput instead of a bare unlock. This is an independent native fix, with
    no upstream implementation copied. The existing Lookup.vtype_conflict
    regression passed even while leaking: 256 repetitions grew vfs.numvnodes
    by 257 with zero FUSE nodes in the isolated pre-fix VM. The new local
    tools/test/linuxulator/guest-fuse-vnode-lifetime.sh additionally checks
    native vnode growth, exact repeat count and FUSE cleanup. The rebuilt
    lifetime2 VM passes all 256 repetitions with native vnodes 80 -> 80,
    zero FUSE nodes, matching hashes and clean shutdown without diagnostics.
    lifetime2-results.json and its manifest/console are retained under
    /usr/obj/5BSD-starnix-fuse-vm-20261010. Native run-6 also passes all 886
    active protocol cases with the corrected module, matching hashes and
    clean shutdown. The core kernel and test binaries match run-5/ATF8.
  - Native FUSE forced-unmount follow-up (2026-10-10): destroy.cc adds
    Destroy.forced_unmount_pending_lookup, releasing a successful LOOKUP
    reply concurrently with a forced unmount and checking request completion
    or cancellation and mount removal. guest-fuse-teardown-stress.sh repeats the race 256
    times in an isolated VM, checking native vnode growth and FUSE cleanup.
    This is locally written lifecycle coverage prompted by the READDIRPLUS
    integration audit, not copied upstream code. It samples scheduling and
    does not establish that every insmntque failure branch was executed.
    First VM run exposed a fixture assumption: native forced purge marks
    the session dead before reclaim, so FORGET/DESTROY delivery is not a
    requirement. The corrected fixture accepts expected daemon ENODEV and
    request ENOTCONN (or EBUSY if mount insertion loses the race). The
    corrected teardown3 VM passes 256 repetitions, native vnodes 80 -> 80,
    zero FUSE nodes and request tickets, exact artifact hashes and clean
    shutdown without diagnostics. Evidence: teardown3-results.json plus its
    manifest/console under /usr/obj/5BSD-starnix-fuse-vm-20261010. Kernel and
    module match lifetime2/run-6; READDIRPLUS teardown remains separate.
  - READDIRPLUS forced-unmount follow-up (2026-10-10): readdir.cc adds
    ReaddirPlus.forced_unmount_pending_reply. The native mock can hold its
    serialized PLUS response while another thread forces unmount. A first
    long-name reply fills most of the user buffer; a second valid two-entry
    wire reply exceeds remaining user capacity, exercising optional prefetch
    during teardown. Checks cover completion/cancellation and mount removal.
    The local teardown stress job now repeats both LOOKUP and PLUS races
    256 times each and checks native vnodes, FUSE nodes and request tickets.
    This extends native integration tests; no upstream code was copied.
    Fixture review/VM failures corrected semaphore lifetime, the native
    minimum read-buffer size and the kernel's maximum requested wire size.
    The corrected teardown8 VM passes 512/512 races, FUSE nodes/tickets zero,
    native vnode growth +4 within the isolated-job limit of 16, exact hashes
    and clean shutdown without diagnostics. Evidence is in teardown8-*.json
    and teardown8-console.log under /usr/obj/5BSD-starnix-fuse-vm-20261010.
    Full native protocol run-10 passes all 888 active cases after the helper
    change, with exact hashes, healthy ZFS and clean shutdown. Its kernel
    and module match run-6; only destroy/readdir test artifacts changed.
  - Earlier regression VM integration follow-up (2026-10-10): the existing
    break_files, break_epoll and break_pidfd ATF wrappers now explicitly
    brand their Linux ELF probes. linux_unshare_test.sh registers the 17
    supported-subset cases already selected by guest-gate.sh plus the native
    capability-mode guard from linux_unshare_capmode.c. Linux-only per-thread
    detachment and shared-table POSIX-lock cases remain reference probes;
    this wrapper does not claim those backends exist. Exec tests receive an
    absolute probe path so chdir does not change the executable under test.
    These are local harness changes around the previously recorded Starnix
    task/descriptor/epoll/waitid test adaptations. No upstream text copied.
    tests/sys/kern/Makefile installs the wrapper and both source files.
    Expanded VM matrix: 11 ATF programs, 49 cases per filesystem. ATF9
    finished at 86/98, with the same six unshare failures on ZFS and tmpfs;
    hashes/filesystems/shutdown verified, guest exit 1. It is not an accepted
    pass. A diagnostic confirmed native shm_seek rejects offsets
    beyond an empty memfd's size. Cwd/exec failures remain under investigation;
